    SuggestedMonth=NULL, IsSystemDefault=1, SortOrder=10120, SourceUrl=N'https://www.muscleandstrength.com/recipes/healthy-protein-strawberry-toaster-strudel', ImageUrl=N'https://cdn.muscleandstrength.com/sites/default/files/field/image/recipe/strawberry-450.jpg', ServingSuggestion=N'Makes one serving.', ContentText=N'Method: Lay out tortilla. Microwave berries and then smash. Add whey protein to strawberries and mix well. Put berry mix in center of tortilla. Fold in sides and top to form a rectangle toaster strudel (use some protein mixed with water as a glue to hold flaps closed). Grill on a George Forman grill for a few minutes, so the outside gets crispy! (Or you could wrap it in parchment paper and put it in an actual toaster, but watch to make sure the paper doesn''t burn!) Mix casein and water - put into a ziplock bag and cut a small corner off. Once toaster strudel is done, pipe the casein mix on top! Let it cool a bit or you''ll burn yourself eating this deliciousness. It seriously tasted exactly like a strawberry toaster strudel.. especially if you let it get crispy enough! If you don''t have casein protein you can always use my go to sweet little mix: 1 TBS whey protein 1 TBS coconut flour 3 TBS water! Enjoy!', CategoriesJson=N'["High Protein Recipes","Breakfast Recipes"]', SourceMacrosJson=N'{"calories_kcal":"114","protein_g":"17","carbs_g":"10.5","fat_g":"4.3"}', ReadCount=18700
